> So, to run under Windows, I should pass "C:\Program Files\Slash'EM\slashem.exe" 
> as server? 

If you use the "Add..." button from the opening dialog, then you should
specify a server type of "Local executable" and then the location of
slashem.exe. The default location for this is:
C:\Program Files\SlashEM\SlashEM 0.0.7e4\slashem.exe
but if you chose to install Slash'EM somewhere else, then you should enter
this instead. Once added, the new connection will appear under the file
scheme.

None of this is necessary if you install Slash'EM in the default location
since the default connection already points to the correct place.

